				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/prlosash" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5257365); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5257365&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238315" alt="PrLosash" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5257365)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/prlosash" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5257365); return false;" >PrLosash</a></span> <span class="odate time_1565795056 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">14 Aug 2019 15:04</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4330534">
									

<div style="text-align: justify;">
<p>I enjoy the idea behind the article and it is quite obvious what the author is trying to achieve with expungements. However, that section is a bit off. I suppose it just doesn't work for me:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Why&nbsp;the&nbsp;expungements&nbsp;don't&nbsp;exactly&nbsp;do&nbsp;the&nbsp;trick&nbsp;for&nbsp;me</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>I initially missed the implication of the SCP-4354-10 tattoo that the tattoos are creating the symbols that they represent, not the image itself. So initially I was like - ok, a Jesus-looking guy is born, not a big deal.</li>
<li>After realizing this implication, I am still not exactly worried. As far as I understand, Jesus is not an established character in the Foundation universe, so what we have is a reality bender and not a very powerful one at that. He can transmute and multiply matter, go through walls and levitate, but it is not like he can destroy the world in the matter of seconds or something. And even if he could, the symbols part comes in and Jesus is generally a benevolent character (as far as I know). So the worst that I could imagine is the Foundation having to kill Jesus, but that's not a big deal.</li>
<li>And if the Jesus is malevolent - the Foundation kinda knows how to contain reality benders and religious figures, so I am not sure why it is a big problem.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, of course, it is a neat idea and execution, I am just not that enamoured with the expungements.</p>
</div>

